Neurodegeneration Mitochondria Lysosomes - License and Usage Notice
======================================================================

Copyright (c) Alexandre Matov. All rights reserved except as granted below.

1. Scope
--------
This repository contains MATLAB and R source code developed by
Alexandre Matov for motion and morphology analysis of mitochondria and
lysosomes, together with a number of bundled third-party utility
functions -- see section 4 below.

2. Permitted use
-----------------
Permission is granted to use, copy, and modify the code in this repository
free of charge for research and educational purposes, provided that:

  a) Any resulting publication, presentation, or derivative work cites
     the relevant publication referenced in README.md;
  b) This notice is retained in copies or substantial portions of the
     code.

Commercial use, redistribution, or incorporation into a commercial
product or service requires prior written permission from Alexandre Matov
(alexandre.matov@gmail.com).

3. No warranty
---------------
This software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express
or implied, including but not limited to the warranties of
merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and noninfringement.
In no event shall the author be liable for any claim, damages, or other
liability arising from the use of this software.

4. Third-party components
--------------------------
This repository bundles the following third-party utilities, none of
which are covered by this notice:

  - `bfopen.m` -- Bio-Formats (Open Microscopy Environment project).
  - `distance2curve.m` -- John D'Errico (MATLAB File Exchange).
  - `getkey.m` -- Jos van der Geest (MATLAB File Exchange).
  - `tofloat.m` -- R.C. Gonzalez, R.E. Woods, S.L. Eddins, from
    "Digital Image Processing Using MATLAB".
  - `filtfilt.m` -- Copyright (C) 1999 Paul Kienzle, licensed under
    the GNU General Public License (see the file's own header); it is
    separately GPL-licensed and not covered by this notice.
  - `hysthresh.m`, `nonmaxsuppts.m`, `normalise.m` -- Peter Kovesi's
    MATLAB/Octave Functions for Computer Vision (University of Western
    Australia).
  - `gm_*.m` (17 files) -- the SDC Morphology Toolbox.
  - `neu_*.m` (6 files) -- third-party neurite-skeletonization
    utilities.
  - `hessianeigs.m` / `meij_hessianeigs.m` -- a commonly-used
    Hessian-eigenvalue snippet from vesselness/Frangi-filter
    implementations.
  - `track.m`, `bpass.m` -- the Crocker/Grier/Weeks particle-tracking
    toolkit (University of Pennsylvania).
